- This resource's noncompliance actions (`scheduledActionsForRule[].scheduledActionConfigurations[].notificationTemplateId`) can reference Microsoft.Graph/notificationMessageTemplates by id. For every such reference present, document it inside the Settings section and wrap the referenced template in `<!-- notifications:start -->` / `<!-- notifications:end -->` markers on their own lines — the same deterministic-splice contract as the assignments block, so it can be re-rendered when a template is renamed without regenerating the page. When a notification-template reference map is provided (a full docs generate-prompt run) resolve each id to the template's display name and link its document; otherwise keep the raw GUID. Never invent a template name, and omit the markers entirely when no action references a template.
